# Argument-count errors from the softcode audit (#2268): PennMUSH's four wordings, chosen by the
# function's declared range, and json()'s own refusal of a wrong count.
::case argc.login
::login wiz Wiz wizpass
think ok

::case argc.forms  one count, two counts, no upper bound, a range
think abs(1,1)
think and()
think extract(a,1,1,|,x)
think mid(a)
think lattr(me,|,x)

::case argc.json  json() refuses a wrong count for its type
think json(string)
think json(number,1,2)
think json(object,a)
think json(null,a,b)
